---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "@fontsource/inter/latin-400.css";
import "@fontsource/inter/latin-500.css";
import "@fontsource/inter/latin-600.css";
import "@fontsource/inter/latin-700.css";
import "@fontsource/plus-jakarta-sans/latin-600.css";
import "@fontsource/plus-jakarta-sans/latin-700.css";
import "@fontsource/plus-jakarta-sans/latin-800.css";
import "../styles/site.css";

// Canonical source: DERIVE.md in peteretelej/uiforagents - keep in sync.
---
<Base title="Derive your own design system - uiforagents" description="uiforagents is a design system factory: when no identity fits, derive a new system from the nearest one - retune the surface, inherit the structure.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 24px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">The factory</p>
      <h1>Derive your own design system</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        uiforagents is a design system factory, not just a catalogue. Two first-class moves:
        use an identity as-is, or - when no identity fits - build a new design system <em>from</em> the nearest one. Never improvise design from scratch; derive.      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>
          Derivation is <strong>single-parent fork-and-retune</strong>. You inherit everything
          structural from one parent identity and retune only its tuning surface. The result is a
          complete, coherent system that is yours - coherent because it inherited a tested one.
        </p>

        <h2 id="the-rule">The rule</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Retune the surface. Inherit the structure. Never restyle components.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Retune:</strong> accent color, neutral tint and hue family, fonts (via the
          documented upgrade path), radius, density, scheme lead (light-first vs dark-first) - and,
          in the artifact lane, the component inventory and class prefix. <strong>Inherit:</strong> component
          structure, spacing and type-scale ratios, the
          prompt-pack's decision logic and do/don'ts, and the lane contracts
          (<code>@layer</code>, <code>light-dark()</code>, no required JavaScript).
        </p>
        <p>
          Every identity's prompt-pack carries a <code>## Tuning surface</code> section: the
          per-identity instance of this rule. Read it first - it names exactly which tokens
          retune and what inherits for that parent.
        </p>

        <h2 id="react-lane">React lane (shadcn/ui)</h2>
        <p>
          Copy the parent's <code>identities/&lt;parent&gt;/</code> directory into your project.
          Retune the theme tokens in <code>theme/theme.css</code> - oklch values only, token names
          never change. Keep <code>overrides/</code> and <code>blocks/</code> as they are; adapt
          content, not styles. Update <code>identity.json</code> with the new name and accent.
        </p>

        <h2 id="artifact-lane">Artifact lane (pure CSS)</h2>
        <p>
          Copy the parent's <code>foundation.css</code> and <code>prompt-pack.md</code>. Retune the
          token block - values only, keep every <code>light-dark()</code> pair ordered light-first.
          Rename the component class prefix to your system's slug (mechanical find-and-replace,
          pack included). Prune components you don't need; add new ones only by the pack's
          conventions: namespaced, inside the <code>@layer foundation</code> block, documented.
          Page CSS stays unlayered and wins without <code>!important</code>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="naming">Naming and provenance</h2>
        <p>
          Name derived systems vibe-derived and brand-neutral - never lab-, person-, or
          client-derived. Record provenance: <code>derived from &lt;parent-slug&gt; vN, &lt;date&gt;</code> in a header comment or
          README.
        </p>

        <h2 id="gates">Gates before you ship</h2>
        <p>
          Run every gate against the derived system, not the parent. Contrast AA on body text and
          key pairs in <strong>both</strong> schemes. Headless check: zero console errors at ~1280px
          and ~390px widths. In the artifact lane, the page must render completely with JavaScript
          disabled; run the print check only if you claim print support. And a one-shot check: an
          agent given only your retuned pack and stylesheet builds identity-faithful pages with no
          improvisation.
        </p>

        <h2 id="promotion">Where derived systems live, and promotion</h2>
        <p>
          Derived systems live in your project. They are <strong>not</strong> added to the
          catalogue automatically - the catalogue stays curated, and that is deliberate. A derived
          system that recurs across projects, or that produces a signature look worth naming, can
          be proposed upstream as an issue on <a href="https://github.com/peteretelej/uiforagents">peteretelej/uiforagents</a>. If
          accepted, it becomes a maintained identity with the full mint gates, a catalogue page,
          and a site card. That is how the catalogue grows.
        </p>

        <p class="note">
          This page mirrors the factory contract (v1). Every catalogue identity's prompt-pack
          now ships its own tuning-surface section; this page, that section, and the parent's
          prompt-pack are the contract. The canonical copy lives in <a href="https://github.com/peteretelej/uiforagents/blob/main/DERIVE.md">DERIVE.md</a> in
          the uiforagents repo.
        </p>

        <p>
          Ready? <a href="/#identities">Pick a parent identity</a> and start from the one closest
          to what you need.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
